1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,239
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,239 --> 00:00:04,640
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,720
[SNORTS]

4
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,319
This is my little brother,
George.

5
00:00:07,319 --> 00:00:08,280
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,520
This is Mummy Pig.

7
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,479
[SNORTS]

8
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,920
And this is Daddy Pig.

9
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:12,879
[SNORTS]

10
00:00:12,879 --> 00:00:13,840
[ALL LAUGHING]

11
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:14,920
Peppa Pig.

12
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,879
[SNORTS]

13
00:00:15,879 --> 00:00:17,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

14
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:19,320
PEPPA:
School Camp.

15
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,880
NARRATOR: Peppa and her friends
are going on a school camp.

16
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,759
[LAUGHING CONTINUES]

17
00:00:24,759 --> 00:00:28,000
Madame Gazelle,
I don't feel very well.

18
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,080
The bus is very bumpy.

19
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,600
NARRATOR: Oh, dear, Pedro Pony
is feeling a bit travel sick.

20
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:34,879
Poor Pedro.

21
00:00:34,879 --> 00:00:37,559
Come and sit in the front
with me.

22
00:00:37,559 --> 00:00:39,199
[GIGGLES]

23
00:00:39,199 --> 00:00:41,120
There. Is that better?

24
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:42,800
A little bit.

25
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,080
Madame Gazelle.

26
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,680
Oh.
Do you feel sick too, Zoe?

27
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,000
I might feel sick later.

28
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,640
Can I sit at the front
just in case?

29
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:54,239
[SNORTS]
Can I sit at the front too?

30
00:00:54,239 --> 00:00:55,760
ALL:
And me.

31
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,960
Ho, ho. I'm sorry, children,

32
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,720
you can't all sit
at the front.

33
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,800
ALL:
Oh.

34
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,120
Never mind.

35
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,560
We're at the campsite now.

36
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:07,080
ALL:
Hooray!

37
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,759
[ALL LAUGHING]

38
00:01:08,759 --> 00:01:10,960
Happy camping, everyone.

39
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,679
ALL:
Bye-bye!

40
00:01:12,679 --> 00:01:16,280
Ho, ho.
This is our campsite.

41
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:20,200
Breathe in the wonderful
fresh air, children.

42
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:23,360
[INHALES DEEPLY
THEN EXHALES AUDIBLY]

43
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:26,200
[ALL INHALE DEEPLY
THEN EXHALE AUDIBLY]

44
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,399
Excellent breathing.

45
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:31,960
Now let's put up our tents.

46
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,399
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends

47
00:01:33,399 --> 00:01:34,640
are putting up their tents.

48
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,720
[ALL LAUGHING]

49
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,800
Children,
you must each find a partner

50
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,720
to share your tent.

51
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,320
Suzy, shall we share a tent?

52
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,440
[BAAS]

53
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,679
I said I'd share with Zoe.

54
00:01:49,679 --> 00:01:52,000
Oh. Sorry, Suzy.

55
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,520
I said I'd share
with Rebecca.

56
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:57,720
Rebecca,
you said you'd share with me.

57
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,679
Oh, yes.

58
00:01:58,679 --> 00:01:59,800
[BAAS]

59
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,720
Emily, who are you going
to share

60
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:02,720
a tent with?

61
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,960
Um...

62
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:06,039
Zoe.
Okay.

63
00:02:06,039 --> 00:02:08,759
Good.
Now you can share with me.

64
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:09,919
Okay.

65
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:12,560
[ALL LAUGHING]

66
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,720
Now I need sticks
to make a campfire.

67
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,519
We'll get sticks.

68
00:02:18,519 --> 00:02:21,079
But me and Pedro
want to get sticks.

69
00:02:21,079 --> 00:02:24,280
Ho, ho.
You can all collect sticks.

70
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,280
[ALL LAUGHING]

71
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:29,680
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends collect
sticks for the campfire.

72
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,680
Wonderful.

73
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,359
[HOOTING]

74
00:02:35,359 --> 00:02:37,120
NARRATOR:
It is nighttime.

75
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,640
Peppa and her friends are
sitting around the campfire.

76
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,480
Children,
let's all sing a song.

77
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:43,519
ALL: Yes!

78
00:02:43,519 --> 00:02:45,679
"The Bing Bong Song,"
please.

79
00:02:45,679 --> 00:02:47,320
Oh, I'm not sure.

80
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:51,239
ALL:
Please, Madame Gazelle.
Sing "The Bing Bong Song."

81
00:02:51,239 --> 00:02:52,920
All right.

82
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,840
♪ Ooh ♪

83
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:58,560
♪ We're playing a tune
And we're singing a song ♪

84
00:02:58,560 --> 00:03:02,519
♪ With a bing and a bong
And a bing ♪

85
00:03:02,519 --> 00:03:04,359
♪ Bong bing boo ♪

86
00:03:04,359 --> 00:03:06,000
♪ Bing bong bing ♪

87
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,679
♪ Bing bong
Bingley bungley boo ♪

88
00:03:09,679 --> 00:03:11,519
♪ Bong bing boo ♪

89
00:03:11,519 --> 00:03:13,200
♪ Bing bong bing ♪

90
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,880
♪ Bing bong
Bingley bungley boo ♪

91
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:18,079
[ALL LAUGHING]

92
00:03:18,079 --> 00:03:22,160
Ho, ho.
Now, children, time for bed.

93
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,519
[ALL LAUGHING]

94
00:03:24,519 --> 00:03:26,399
Good night, children.

95
00:03:26,399 --> 00:03:28,679
ALL:
Goodnight, Madame Gazelle.

96
00:03:28,679 --> 00:03:29,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

97
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,920
NARRATOR:
Peppa and Suzy

98
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,000
are in their sleeping bags.

99
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,440
I've got a torch.

100
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,799
Me too.

101
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

102
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:46,799
Attention, children.
No more giggling, please.

103
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:51,799
[HOOTING]

104
00:03:51,799 --> 00:03:54,320
What was that funny noise?

105
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,920
I don't know.

106
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,679
[HOOTING CONTINUES]

107
00:03:57,679 --> 00:03:59,480
There it is again.

108
00:04:00,959 --> 00:04:03,839
Suzy, where are you going?

109
00:04:03,839 --> 00:04:06,399
Madame Gazelle.

110
00:04:06,399 --> 00:04:08,560
I'm a bit scared.

111
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,280
Oh,
would you like to come in?

112
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,679
Yes, please.

113
00:04:12,679 --> 00:04:14,560
Madame Gazelle.

114
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:17,760
I think
I'm a bit scared too.

115
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,560
Can I come in, please?

116
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,920
Of course.

117
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:22,120
[GIGGLES]

118
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:25,159
I think
I might be scared later.

119
00:04:25,159 --> 00:04:27,120
I might be scared later too.

120
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,360
BOTH:
And me.

121
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,440
Come in, everyone.

122
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,520
[ALL LAUGHING]

123
00:04:34,039 --> 00:04:36,880
PEPPA: Can we have
"The Bing Bong Song," please?

124
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,200
MADAME GAZELLE:
All right.

125
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,039
♪ We're playing a tune ♪

126
00:04:40,039 --> 00:04:41,640
♪ And we're singing a song ♪

127
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:45,919
♪ With a bing and a bong
and a bing ♪♪

128
00:04:48,719 --> 00:04:51,039
PEPPA:
Captain Daddy Pig.

129
00:04:51,039 --> 00:04:53,840
NARRATOR: Peppa and her family
are borrowing Grandpa's boat

130
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,880
for the day.

131
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,719
[SNORTS]
Remember, Daddy Pig,

132
00:04:56,719 --> 00:05:01,120
push the lever forward
to go forward.

133
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:03,000
Aye, aye, Grandpa Pig.

134
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Forward.

135
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,159
And back to go back.

136
00:05:07,159 --> 00:05:09,440
And back. Simple.

137
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,400
And please
look after my boat.

138
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,640
I've just had it painted.

139
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:17,919
Oh, Grandpa Pig,
what an old fusspot you are.

140
00:05:17,919 --> 00:05:19,719
[ALL LAUGHING]

141
00:05:19,719 --> 00:05:20,760
Are my crew ready?

142
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,000
ALL:
Yes, Captain Daddy Pig.

143
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,080
Then let's go.

144
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:27,599
NARRATOR: Oh,
the boat is moving backwards.

145
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:31,640
Aah!
Watch out for the bridge.

146
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,640
Oops.

147
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:35,240
Oh, that was close.

148
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,159
Bye-bye.

149
00:05:36,159 --> 00:05:37,240
ALL:
Bye-bye.

150
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,880
Have a lovely time.

151
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,520
[SNORTS]
I hope my boat comes back

152
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,680
in one piece.

153
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,960
Stop worrying.

154
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,320
It will be fine.

155
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,599
[♪♪♪]

156
00:05:47,599 --> 00:05:49,680
Peppa, ring the bell.

157
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,400
Aye, aye, Captain Daddy.

158
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,479
[BELL RINGING]

159
00:05:52,479 --> 00:05:54,560
[ALL LAUGHING]

160
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:57,800
[SNORTS]
I'm a bit hungry.

161
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,159
So am I.

162
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:01,800
Grandpa's left us a picnic,
in the galley.

163
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,080
What's a galley?

164
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:06,120
A galley
is a boat's little kitchen.

165
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:07,159
Follow me.

166
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:08,400
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George

167
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,599
are going inside the boat.

168
00:06:09,599 --> 00:06:11,599
BOTH: Wow.

169
00:06:11,599 --> 00:06:13,800
What a tiny little kitchen.

170
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,760
[SNORTS]
Where's the picnic?

171
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:18,000
The obvious place
would be here.

172
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,280
[DADDY PIG GRUNTS
THEN PEPPA GIGGLES]

173
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:22,400
That's not a picnic.

174
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:25,080
Then it must be here.

175
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,280
And that's not a picnic.

176
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,479
This kitchen has everything
in the wrong place.

177
00:06:30,479 --> 00:06:32,159
Wow, a TV.
[CAR ENGINES WHIRRING]

178
00:06:32,159 --> 00:06:34,280
NARRATOR: Daddy Pig
cannot find the picnic.

179
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:35,840
It's impossible.

180
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:38,440
[SNORTS]
If this was my kitchen,

181
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:41,359
the picnic would be here.

182
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:43,039
Oh. Well done, Peppa.

183
00:06:43,039 --> 00:06:44,880
NARRATOR:
Peppa has found the picnic.

184
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,960
[ALL LAUGHING]

185
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:50,359
Delicious.

186
00:06:50,359 --> 00:06:51,680
[DUCKS QUACKING]

187
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,799
Oh, it's the ducks.
[QUACKS]

188
00:06:53,799 --> 00:06:56,840
Hello, Mrs. Duck.
Would you like some bread?

189
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:58,159
[DUCKS QUACKING]
[BOTH LAUGHING]

190
00:06:58,159 --> 00:06:59,400
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George

191
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,320
love feeding bread
to ducks.

192
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,440
[DUCKS QUACKING]

193
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:04,840
Look out. Long reeds ahead.

194
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:08,680
Don't worry, Grandpa's boat
will easily go through them.

195
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,760
[ENGINE CREAKING]

196
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:13,840
Are we stuck?

197
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,039
No. We can reverse.

198
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,680
Now, are we stuck?
Yes.

199
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:23,080
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear, Grandpa's boat
is stuck in the reeds.

200
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:25,440
I'll just give it
a little push.

201
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:28,680
Do be careful, Daddy Pig.

202
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,520
I know what I'm doing.

203
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,960
When I say "Go,"
start the engine.

204
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,080
ALL:
Aye, aye, Captain Daddy Pig.

205
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:36,239
Go.

206
00:07:36,239 --> 00:07:38,400
[ENGINE STARTS
THEN DADDY PIG GRUNTS]

207
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:41,479
NARRATOR: Daddy Pig has pushed
the boat out of the reeds.

208
00:07:41,479 --> 00:07:42,640
ALL:
Hooray!

209
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,640
[SNORTS]
Quick, Daddy!

210
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,400
Jump back on the boat!
[PANTING]

211
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,719
NARRATOR: Oh, no,
Daddy Pig is being left behind.

212
00:07:50,719 --> 00:07:53,359
Swim faster, Daddy.

213
00:07:53,359 --> 00:07:55,159
Stop the engine.

214
00:07:55,159 --> 00:07:56,320
What's he saying?

215
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,960
[MUFFLED]
Stop the engine.

216
00:07:57,960 --> 00:08:02,039
Daddy says,
"Stop the engine."

217
00:08:02,039 --> 00:08:03,479
Oh.

218
00:08:03,479 --> 00:08:04,599
[PANTING]

219
00:08:04,599 --> 00:08:06,679
MUMMY PIG:
Are you okay, Daddy Pig?

220
00:08:06,679 --> 00:08:08,560
Yes, I'm fine.

221
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,039
But let's head for home

222
00:08:10,039 --> 00:08:12,200
before we have
any more adventures.

223
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,280
ALL:
Aye, aye, Captain Daddy Pig.

224
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:16,039
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

225
00:08:16,039 --> 00:08:18,239
They've been gone for ages.

226
00:08:18,239 --> 00:08:20,599
I hope my boat's all right.

227
00:08:20,599 --> 00:08:21,640
[BELL RINGING]

228
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,400
Look, there they are.

229
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:24,479
[BELL RINGING]

230
00:08:24,479 --> 00:08:25,960
ALL: Hello.
BOTH: Ahoy there.

231
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,919
[BOTH GIGGLING]

232
00:08:26,919 --> 00:08:29,120
I'll just park the boat.

233
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,239
[LAUGHS]

234
00:08:30,239 --> 00:08:34,600
You park a car,
but you moor a boat.

235
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,319
I'll show you.

236
00:08:36,319 --> 00:08:38,559
NARRATOR: Grandpa Pig
is going to moor the boat.

237
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:40,959
[SNORTS]
The secret of mooring

238
00:08:40,959 --> 00:08:43,439
is to do it carefully.

239
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:46,280
Mind the bridge.
What?

240
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:48,199
ALL:
Look behind you.

241
00:08:48,199 --> 00:08:49,120
Aah!

242
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:52,439
[♪♪♪]

243
00:08:52,439 --> 00:08:56,360
Oh.
I didn't mean to do that.

244
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:59,280
Grandpa has broken his boat.

245
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,800
Never mind, Grandpa.

246
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:03,600
You can have lots of fun
mending it.

247
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,959
It is true
that I love mending things.

248
00:09:06,959 --> 00:09:09,439
Can I help mend the boat,
Grandpa?

249
00:09:09,439 --> 00:09:12,720
Ho, ho.
Of course you can, Peppa.

250
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,800
[ALL LAUGHING]

251
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,040
[♪♪♪]

252
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:22,199
PEPPA:
The Power Cut.

253
00:09:22,199 --> 00:09:24,199
NARRATOR: It is evening. 
[ROCK MUSIC
PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

254
00:09:24,199 --> 00:09:26,319
Peppa and George
are in the sitting room,

255
00:09:26,319 --> 00:09:28,560
dancing
to their favorite song.

256
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:32,560
Daddy Pig is in the hallway
vacuuming the carpet.

257
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:35,160
And Mummy Pig
is in her study

258
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:38,120
doing important work
on her computer.

259
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,120
Oh.

260
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,720
[MUSIC STOPS]

261
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:41,800
Oh.

262
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,120
Oh.

263
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,439
Mommy, Daddy,
it's gone all dark

264
00:09:47,439 --> 00:09:49,520
and the music is broken.

265
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,480
And my vacuum won't work.

266
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,560
And my computer
has switched off.

267
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:55,439
BOTH: Ooh.

268
00:09:55,439 --> 00:09:57,360
NARRATOR: Mummy Pig
tries the light switch,

269
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,360
but the lights
do not come on.

270
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,319
It must be a power cut.

271
00:10:01,319 --> 00:10:03,240
[SNORTS]
What's a power cut?

272
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,720
A power cut
is when there is no electricity.

273
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:08,600
What's electric-kity?

274
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:11,959
Electricity
is what makes everything

275
00:10:11,959 --> 00:10:13,480
in our house work.

276
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,040
Will the electric-kity
come back again?

277
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,400
Yes.
[SNORTS]

278
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:20,280
But in the meantime,
we need to find a torch.

279
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,400
I think there's a torch
in the cellar.

280
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:25,199
Okay, I'll go and get it.

281
00:10:25,199 --> 00:10:27,000
Will you be okay, Daddy?

282
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,640
Ho, ho, I'll be fine.

283
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:32,000
I can see very well
in the dark.

284
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,240
[CLANGING AND HONKING]

285
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:34,800
Who put that there?

286
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,760
Oh.
Daddy, are you okay?

287
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,800
DADDY PIG: Yes,
it's just a bit dark down here.

288
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,880
[CLANGING AND CRASHING]

289
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:44,640
Oh, I've just remembered.

290
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,760
I think the torch
is in the kitchen.

291
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:49,560
[PEPPA AND GEORGE GIGGLING]

292
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:51,160
Ah-ha.

293
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,800
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig has found the torch.

294
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:55,600
Can I hold the torch, Mummy?
Okay.

295
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,640
[GIGGLES]

296
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,680
George.

297
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,839
Look at me.

298
00:10:59,839 --> 00:11:02,120
NARRATOR:
Peppa is making a funny face.

299
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,480
[CRYING]

300
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:06,280
Don't worry, George,
it's only Peppa.

301
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,439
[ALL LAUGH]

302
00:11:08,439 --> 00:11:12,120
Oh, we'd better tell Daddy
we found the torch.

303
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,480
[OBJECTS CLANGING]

304
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,240
NARRATOR:
Daddy is still in the cellar,

305
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,520
looking for the torch.

306
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,360
I'm sure it's here
somewhere.

307
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:22,400
PEPPA:
Daddy, we found the torch.

308
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:26,079
Luckily, it was in the kitchen
all the time.

309
00:11:26,079 --> 00:11:28,000
What a stroke of luck.

310
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
[LAUGHS]

311
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,160
[SNORTS]
Now we just have to wait

312
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,719
until the electricity
comes back.

313
00:11:33,719 --> 00:11:36,920
How long will that be
exactly?

314
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:41,040
Um, I would say,
exactly a long time.

315
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,319
BOTH:
Oh.

316
00:11:42,319 --> 00:11:46,360
But George and I
want to do some dancing.

317
00:11:48,319 --> 00:11:50,480
[SNORTS]
I know what we can do.

318
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,760
We can watch
some television.

319
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,120
Oh, it won't go on.

320
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,480
[MUMMY PIG AND DADDY PIG
LAUGH]

321
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:00,560
[SNORTS]
The TV needs electricity too.

322
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:01,560
Does it?

323
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,719
BOTH: Yes.

324
00:12:02,719 --> 00:12:06,079
Oh.
Now what are we going to do?

325
00:12:06,079 --> 00:12:08,920
In the olden days,
when there was no television,

326
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,600
children would have to make up
their own games.

327
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,600
Hm. I know.

328
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,920
[SNORTS]
I need a cardboard box.

329
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,000
NARRATOR:
What is Peppa doing?

330
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,600
[SNORTS]
Mommy, will you cut a hole

331
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,959
in this box for me?

332
00:12:21,959 --> 00:12:24,439
What for?
You'll see.

333
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,280
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig is cutting a hole

334
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,600
in the cardboard box.

335
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:29,959
There you are, Peppa.

336
00:12:29,959 --> 00:12:31,120
Thank you.

337
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,959
Now, you all have
to sit down there.

338
00:12:33,959 --> 00:12:37,640
And, George, you have to point
this torch at me.

339
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:38,599
[SNORTS]

340
00:12:38,599 --> 00:12:41,280
[GIGGLING]

341
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:42,760
[CLEARS THROAT]

342
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:47,800
Welcome to Peppa Pig News
with me, Peppa Pig.

343
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,319
[ALL LAUGH]

344
00:12:49,319 --> 00:12:51,360
NARRATOR: Peppa has made
her own television.

345
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:53,560
[SNORTS]
Today, the whole world

346
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:54,839
stopped working

347
00:12:54,839 --> 00:12:56,360
when there was a power cut,

348
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:59,719
and all the electric-kity
was lost.

349
00:12:59,719 --> 00:13:00,920
[ALL LAUGH]

350
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,680
Very good, Peppa.

351
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:05,599
Daddy Pig says
that the electric-kity

352
00:13:05,599 --> 00:13:09,280
won't be back
for a long, long time.

353
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,439
ALL: Oh.

354
00:13:10,439 --> 00:13:12,000
NARRATOR:
The electricity is back.

355
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,599
ALL: Hooray!
Shush, I haven't finished yet.

356
00:13:15,599 --> 00:13:17,800
[SNORTS]
Switch the lights off.

357
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,520
Okay, Peppa.

358
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,760
Good.

359
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:21,880
Ahem.

360
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:24,599
I have
some very important news.

361
00:13:24,599 --> 00:13:29,120
The queen has just found
some more electric-kity,

362
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,920
and says that everyone
can now be happy again.

363
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,880
Very good, Peppa.

364
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:36,599
ALL:
Hooray!

365
00:13:36,599 --> 00:13:38,199
Let's dance.

366
00:13:38,199 --> 00:13:39,880
[ROCK MUSIC PLAYING
AND PEPPA LAUGHING]

367
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:41,439
[ALL LAUGHING]

368
00:13:41,439 --> 00:13:43,360
NARRATOR: Peppa quite enjoyed
the power cut,

369
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:47,240
but she's happy
the electricity is back again.

370
00:13:49,439 --> 00:13:50,839
PEPPA:
Bouncy Ball.

371
00:13:50,839 --> 00:13:53,000
[♪♪♪]

372
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,480
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

373
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:56,120
[BOTH LAUGHING]

374
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,959
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are going to play

375
00:13:57,959 --> 00:14:00,319
in the garden
with their ball.

376
00:14:00,319 --> 00:14:01,400
Whee!

377
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,839
NARRATOR:
George throws the ball

378
00:14:02,839 --> 00:14:04,520
as high as he can

379
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,760
and catches it.

380
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,920
[GIGGLES]

381
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:09,240
[SNORTS]
I can do that too.

382
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,640
Whee!

383
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,880
Oh.

384
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,520
NARRATOR:
Peppa has missed the ball.

385
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,319
[GIGGLES]
This is a silly game.

386
00:14:18,319 --> 00:14:19,680
[BICYCLE BELL RINGING]

387
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,079
[BAAS]

388
00:14:21,079 --> 00:14:22,839
NARRATOR:
Here is Peppa's best friend,

389
00:14:22,839 --> 00:14:23,959
Suzy Sheep.

390
00:14:23,959 --> 00:14:25,640
Suzy has two
tennis rackets.

391
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:26,599
Hello, Peppa.

392
00:14:26,599 --> 00:14:28,240
[SNORTS]
Hello, Suzy.

393
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,199
Let's play tennis.

394
00:14:30,199 --> 00:14:32,520
Yes, that sounds fun.

395
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,439
[SNORTS]
To you, Suzy.

396
00:14:36,719 --> 00:14:37,920
Oh.

397
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:39,599
NARRATOR:
Suzy has missed the ball.

398
00:14:39,599 --> 00:14:41,400
[GIGGLES]

399
00:14:44,439 --> 00:14:45,680
Oh.

400
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:48,520
NARRATOR:
Peppa has missed the ball.

401
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:50,040
[BOTH LAUGHING]

402
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:52,400
NARRATOR: Peppa and Suzy
like playing tennis,

403
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:55,000
but George feels
a bit left out.

404
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,520
[CRYING]

405
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:59,680
Oh. Sorry, George.

406
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:01,760
You can't play tennis.

407
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:04,319
We only have two rackets.

408
00:15:04,319 --> 00:15:06,120
[SOBS]

409
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,199
I know.

410
00:15:07,199 --> 00:15:09,640
George can be the ball boy.

411
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:13,560
Yes. It's a very important job.
[SNORTS]

412
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:15,640
NARRATOR: George is going
to be the ball boy.

413
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:19,000
He has to collect the ball
when it is hit too far.

414
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,240
To you, Suzy.

415
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,319
Oh, missed it.

416
00:15:23,319 --> 00:15:24,839
BOTH:
Ball boy.

417
00:15:24,839 --> 00:15:26,800
[GEORGE SNORTS THEN GIGGLES]

418
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,199
[PANTING]

419
00:15:32,199 --> 00:15:34,800
Thank you, ball boy.

420
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,839
Oh.

421
00:15:35,839 --> 00:15:37,640
BOTH:
Ball boy.

422
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:38,880
[GEORGE PANTING]

423
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:47,000
Thank you, ball boy.

424
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,079
BOTH:
Ball boy.

425
00:15:49,079 --> 00:15:51,280
[CRYING]

426
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:54,920
NARRATOR: Oh, dear.
George doesn't like this game.

427
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:56,560
[BICYCLE BELLS RINGING]

428
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,680
[ALL LAUGHING]

429
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:59,040
NARRATOR:
Here are Danny Dog,

430
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:00,280
Pedro Pony, Candy Cat,

431
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,959
Rebecca Rabbit,
and Richard Rabbit.

432
00:16:01,959 --> 00:16:03,920
Hello, everyone.
ALL: Hello.

433
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:06,319
[SNORTS]
We're playing tennis.

434
00:16:06,319 --> 00:16:07,800
Can we play too?

435
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,240
But there aren't
enough racquets.

436
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,240
ALL: Oh.

437
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,880
Let's play something else.

438
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:15,319
[BARKS]
Let's play football.

439
00:16:15,319 --> 00:16:17,359
ALL:
Yes, football.

440
00:16:17,359 --> 00:16:19,920
[SNORTS]
Girls against boys.

441
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,760
[ALL LAUGHING]

442
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:24,000
We each need a goalkeeper.

443
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,199
Me, me.
Me, me.

444
00:16:26,199 --> 00:16:30,240
NARRATOR:
Pedro Pony and Rebecca Rabbit
will be the goalkeepers.

445
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,439
We'll start.

446
00:16:31,439 --> 00:16:33,400
[GIGGLES]

447
00:16:34,719 --> 00:16:36,800
[SQUEAKING THEN GIGGLING]

448
00:16:39,479 --> 00:16:41,079
BOTH:
Goal!

449
00:16:41,079 --> 00:16:43,479
NARRATOR: Richard Rabbit
has scored a goal.

450
00:16:43,479 --> 00:16:45,079
The boys are winning.

451
00:16:45,079 --> 00:16:46,120
[BOTH LAUGH]

452
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,560
That's not fair.

453
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:49,319
We weren't ready.

454
00:16:49,319 --> 00:16:51,240
[GIGGLES]

455
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,120
Hey, that's cheating.

456
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,959
You can't hold the ball.

457
00:16:54,959 --> 00:16:57,719
Yes, I can,
I'm the goalkeeper.

458
00:16:57,719 --> 00:16:59,319
ALL:
Go, Rebecca, go!

459
00:16:59,319 --> 00:17:00,719
Oof.

460
00:17:00,719 --> 00:17:01,880
Goal.

461
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,240
ALL GIRLS:
Hooray!

462
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,280
The goal is not allowed.

463
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,440
ALL:
Yes, it is.

464
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,480
ALL:
No, it isn't.

465
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,560
ALL:
Yes, it is.

466
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,480
What a lot of noise.

467
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:13,079
Daddy,
the boys are cheating.

468
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:14,760
No, the girls are cheating.

469
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:18,079
It sounds like
you need a referee.

470
00:17:18,079 --> 00:17:19,960
What's a referee?

471
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:23,200
It's someone who makes sure
that everyone plays fair.

472
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,240
ALL:
I'll be the referee! Me, me, me!

473
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,639
Stop, stop!

474
00:17:26,639 --> 00:17:27,960
[BLOWS WHISTLE]

475
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,760
I'll be the referee.

476
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:32,520
[SNORTS]
The next team to get a goal

477
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:33,919
will win the game.

478
00:17:33,919 --> 00:17:35,520
ALL: Hooray!

479
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,600
[BLOWS WHISTLE]

480
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,480
[SNORTS]
Where's the ball?

481
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,919
[BOTH GIGGLING]

482
00:17:40,919 --> 00:17:42,879
Quick, score a goal.

483
00:17:42,879 --> 00:17:44,560
Stop them.

484
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:46,600
[GIGGLING CONTINUES]

485
00:17:49,919 --> 00:17:51,280
Oof.

486
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,560
Goal!

487
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,600
[BLOWS WHISTLE]

488
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:56,240
Richard Rabbit
has scored a goal.

489
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,480
ALL: Hooray!

490
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:59,120
The boys win.

491
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,399
ALL: Oh.

492
00:18:00,399 --> 00:18:02,480
Football is a silly game.

493
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:04,120
Just a moment.

494
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,760
The boys scored
in their own goal.

495
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:08,919
That means the girls win.

496
00:18:08,919 --> 00:18:09,840
Really?

497
00:18:09,840 --> 00:18:11,280
ALL:
Hooray!

498
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:13,440
Football is a great game.

499
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,520
[ALL LAUGHING]

500
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,040
[♪♪♪]

501
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:21,080
[GIGGLING AND SNORTING]

502
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,960
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

503
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:25,679
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

504
00:18:25,679 --> 00:18:27,480
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

505
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,840
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

506
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,840
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

507
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,879
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

